          "lem-complex-algebraic-stratifications-have-finite-conical-cochain-models",
          "lem-finite-simplicial-constructible-sheaves-have-a-derived-incidence-model",
          "thm-compactly-supported-derived-pushforward-has-exceptional-inverse-image-adjoint",
          "thm-extension-by-zero-adjunction-exactness"
        ],
        "statement": "Assume AC and the actual finite conical/triangulation and derived-incidence-model suppliers listed below. On the analytic space $X$ of a separated finite-type complex algebraic variety, constructible complexes admit the fixed-space finite models required by those suppliers. Then $\\omega_X=a_X^!k$ and $D_X=R\\mathcal Hom(-,\\omega_X)$ preserve bounded constructible objects and the natural evaluation $A\\to D_XD_XA$ is an isomorphism. On a smooth complex $d$-variety, the complex orientation normalizes $\\omega_X\\simeq k_X[2d]$. For constructible maps for which the geometric supplier proves the stated bounded outputs, $Rf_*D_X\\simeq D_YRf_!$, $D_YRf_*\\simeq Rf_!D_X$, and $f^!\\simeq D_Xf^*D_Y$. Proper base change has the coherent extraordinary dual exchange $u^!Rf_*\\simeq Rf'_*v^!$. The fixed-space triangulation is not an assumed globally simplicial model of $f$.",
        "strategy": "Assume AC. Sources: Verdier, expose 300, SS2 p. 341-343 (the candidate $f^!$ and the trace), SS3 pp. 343-345 (the duality theorem, proved on generators $A_V$ and then by descent), SS1.1-SS1.4 pp. 339-341 (localization; compact support; finite dimension); BBD, Faisceaux pervers, SS1.4.1-1.4.10 (recollement localization triangles) and SS2.1.1-2.1.7 (perversity on stratified spaces), as an independent treatment of the local intermediate-extension construction; Bernstein-Lunts, Part I SS1.6.1-1.6.3 (dualizing object and Verdier duality $Df_!=f_*D$, $f^!D=Df^*$). Step 1: dualizing transitivity $f^!\\omega_Y\\simeq\\omega_X$ is computed on local section complexes $R\\Gamma(U,f^!\\omega_Y)=R\\mathrm{Hom}_Y(Rf_!j_{U!}k,\\omega_Y)\\simeq R\\mathrm{Hom}_k(R\\Gamma_c(U,k),k)=R\\Gamma(U,\\omega_X)$, using the exceptional-adjunction Hom formula and compact-support composition, and $R\\Gamma(U,D_XA)=R\\mathrm{Hom}_k(R\\Gamma_c(U,A),k)$; over a field the injective coefficient is $k$, so this is the signed dual cochain model with no integral Ext correction. Step 2: on an oriented real $n$-manifold the compact-support cochains of a small ball have one generator in degree $n$ normalized by the positive orientation (finite relative cellular model of the closed simplex, with excision), so $\\omega_X\\simeq or_X[n]$ and complex orientation trivializes $or_X$ to give $k_X[2d]$ on a smooth complex $d$-variety. Step 3: for a finite-rank local system $L$ on a smooth stratum, $D_XL\\simeq L^\\vee[n]$ and finite-dimensional double-dual evaluation is an isomorphism; the boundary-link induction may not assume $DD(j_!L)=j_!DD(L)$. Step 4: choose a finite regular triangulation $P$ with deleted subcomplex $L$ modelling $X$, subordinate to the constructible datum (geometric supplier); the derived-incidence supplier identifies the bounded derived category of finite face diagrams with the constructible subcategory, with injective cogenerators $I_\\sigma$ given by $k$ on the closed simplex extended by zero. Step 5: compute $D_XI_\\sigma=j_{\\mathrm{int}\\sigma!}k[\\dim\\sigma]$ and its inverse on a star by the finite relative cellular model of a half-line times a disk; evaluation $I_\\sigma\\to D_XD_XI_\\sigma$ is ordinary finite-dimensional double-dual evaluation and is an isomorphism; finite injective incidence resolutions propagate this through cones, proving $A\\to D_XD_XA$ for all bounded constructible $A$ and bounded constructibility of $D_X$. Step 6: after biduality, $Rf_*D_XA\\simeq D_YRf_!A$ (both represent $R\\mathcal Hom(Rf_!A,\\omega_Y)$ with source-side $D_XA$), applying $D_Y$ gives $D_YRf_*\\simeq Rf_!D_X$, and the transpositions $\\operatorname{Hom}(A,D_Xf^*D_YB)\\simeq\\operatorname{Hom}(f^*D_YB,D_XA)\\simeq\\operatorname{Hom}(Rf_!A,B)$ identify $f^!\\simeq D_Xf^*D_Y$ on the bounded constructible category; proper base change dualizes to $u^!Rf_*\\simeq Rf'_*v^!$. Pasting coherence follows from naturality of the evaluation and the sectionwise base-change maps.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Jean-Louis Verdier, Dualite dans la cohomologie des espaces localement compacts, Seminaire N. Bourbaki 1964-1966, expose 300, pp. 337-349 (Novembre 1965)",
              "url": "https://www.numdam.org/item/SB_1964-1966__9__337_0.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "A. A. Beilinson, J. Bernstein, P. Deligne, Faisceaux pervers, Asterisque 100 (1982); SS1.4 recollement t-structures and SS2.1 perverse sheaves on stratified spaces",
              "url": "https://www.numdam.org/item/AST_1982__100__1_0.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "J. Bernstein, V. Lunts, Equivariant Sheaves and Functors, Part I SS1.4-SS1.8 (six operations, Verdier duality, smooth maps and smooth base change) and SS1.9 with Appendices A (acyclic maps)",
              "url": "https://www.math.tau.ac.il/~bernstei/Publication_list/publication_texts/luntz_ESF/3-derived-category-and-functors.pdf"
            }
          ]
        },
        "axiom_use": "AC is assumed and consumed through the geometric finite-stratification/triangulation suppliers ([[lem-complex-algebraic-stratifications-have-finite-conical-cochain-models]] and [[lem-finite-simplicial-constructible-sheaves-have-a-derived-incidence-model]], both AC-stated), through the injective/incidence models of the ordinary-operations and exceptional-adjunction suppliers, and through [[lem-analytic-six-operation-support-and-trace-calculus]]. The local cellular dual computations and the orientation normalization are choice-free.",
        "dependency_level": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-analytic-sheaf-six-operations-have-coherent-base-change-projection-and-trace",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Coherent six operations on analytic constructible field sheaves",
        "deps": [
          "def-algebraically-constructible-complex-of-analytic-field-sheaves",
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-c-soft-sheaf",
          "def-compactly-supported-global-sections",
          "def-derived-category-of-an-abelian-category",
          "def-derived-hom-in-the-bounded-setting",
          "def-derived-operations-on-analytic-sheaves-over-locally-compact-spaces",
          "def-direct-image-sheaf",
          "def-extension-by-zero-abelian-sheaf",
          "def-inverse-image-presheaf-and-sheaf",
          "def-locally-constant-sheaf-of-finite-rank",
          "def-sheaf-hom",
          "def-sheaf-on-topological-space",
          "def-sheaf-tensor-product",
          "lem-analytic-six-operation-support-and-trace-calculus",
          "lem-complex-algebraic-stratifications-have-finite-conical-cochain-models",
          "lem-finite-simplicial-constructible-sheaves-have-a-derived-incidence-model",
          "lem-locally-contractible-metric-spaces-have-singular-constant-sheaf-cohomology",
          "thm-verdier-duality-on-oriented-stratified-complex-varieties"
        ],
        "statement": "Assume AC and the actual geometric and derived-incidence suppliers of the Verdier theorem. For analytic algebraic maps on its proved constructible subcategory, the six operations $f^*,Rf_*,Rf_!,f^!,\\otimes_k^L,R\\mathcal Hom$ have their three adjunctions, composition and identity comparisons, ordinary proper and extraordinary proper base change, projection formula, support localization, dualizing transitivity and trace. The comparisons commute with Cartesian pasting, composition of maps, evaluation and trace, giving a coherent pull-push product calculus. For a locally trivial product projection with finite-type smooth fibre $F$, the actual finite product cochain model gives $R\\mathrm{pr}_*\\mathrm{pr}^*B\\simeq B\\otimes_k C^*(F;k)$, with its ordinary unit. Smooth base change for $Rf_*$ holds whenever a supplied factorization $f=p\\circ j$ has $p$ proper and $j$ an open inclusion with the conical local models below; proper maps already satisfy it. Their finite constructible models commute with extension of coefficient fields. Geometric output preservation is the exact geometric supplier, not an additional axiom.",
        "strategy": "Assume AC. Sources: Verdier, expose 300, SS1.2 p. 340 (base change), SS1.5 p. 341 (composition), SS5 p. 348 (submersive maps and the projection formula for a product projection); Stacks Project, Cohomology of Sheaves SS17-SS18 (base-change map and proper base change) and SS54 (projection formula Lemma 54.2); Bernstein-Lunts, Part I SS1.8 (smooth base change and compatibility with all functors). Step 1: apply the support-and-trace lemma to the actual analytic maps; its proper-support section and injective models give ordinary exchange, the projection formula, both support-localization triangles, canonical composition, units and traces, all as section-level identities carried through the same resolution comparisons. Step 2: apply the constructible Verdier theorem to the actual finite conical/incidence models; it supplies duality, orientation and the extraordinary exchange by dualizing the canonical proper base-change map, and functoriality carries pasting and trace squares to their dual squares, while the tensor-Hom and inverse/direct-image adjunctions are the signed dg comparisons of the ordinary-operations lemma. Step 3 (product projection): tensor the finite base diagram resolution with the fibre constant-diagram resolution ([[lem-finite-simplicial-constructible-sheaves-have-a-derived-incidence-model]]); each realized term has support a product of closed cells minus deleted faces, and its intersection with a small base star times $F$ has contractible factors, so the constant-sheaf comparison [[lem-locally-contractible-metric-spaces-have-singular-constant-sheaf-cohomology]] makes it section-acyclic; applying sections gives the natural finite double complex $B|_{\\mathrm{star}}\\otimes C^*(F;k)$ and identifies the derived image and its unit with $B\\otimes C^*(F;k)$ and $B\\otimes(k\\to C^*(F;k))$. For smooth base change of an open inclusion $j$, a local smooth chart is a product with a contractible ball, and the boundary-star section model becomes the old finite cochain model tensored with the ball cochains, whose augmentation is a quasi-isomorphism by an explicit contraction. If the supplied $f=p\\circ j$ has $p$ proper, combine this exchange with the constructed proper base-change map for $p$; compatibility with composition identifies the composite with the canonical $f$ exchange. No compactification existence theorem is inferred: the clause applies only to the stated supplied factorization. Step 4 (coefficient extension): use the geometric supplier's finite local cellular/cochain models; scalar extension is exact on vector spaces, commutes with finite sums, cohomology and finite-dimensional duals, so ordinary inverse image, finite cochain pushforward, tensor, internal Hom and the support-defined Verdier comparisons extend termwise, and the exceptional comparison follows from $f^!=D_Xf^*D_Y$; no infinite product of injective stalks is involved.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Jean-Louis Verdier, Dualite dans la cohomologie des espaces localement compacts, Seminaire N. Bourbaki 1964-1966, expose 300, pp. 337-349 (Novembre 1965)",
              "url": "https://www.numdam.org/item/SB_1964-1966__9__337_0.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "The Stacks Project, Cohomology of Sheaves (chapter 20): SS12 Flasque sheaves, SS16 Cohomology on Hausdorff quasi-compact spaces, SS17 The base change map, SS18 Proper base change in topology, SS21 Cohomology with support in a closed subset, SS54 Projection formula",
              "url": "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/download/cohomology.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "J. Bernstein, V. Lunts, Equivariant Sheaves and Functors, Part I SS1.4-SS1.8 (six operations, Verdier duality, smooth maps and smooth base change) and SS1.9 with Appendices A (acyclic maps)",
              "url": "https://www.math.tau.ac.il/~bernstei/Publication_list/publication_texts/luntz_ESF/3-derived-category-and-functors.pdf"
            }
          ]
        },
        "axiom_use": "AC is assumed and consumed through the geometric suppliers [[lem-complex-algebraic-stratifications-have-finite-conical-cochain-models]], [[lem-finite-simplicial-constructible-sheaves-have-a-derived-incidence-model]] and [[lem-locally-contractible-metric-spaces-have-singular-constant-sheaf-cohomology]], and through the injective/incidence models of the support-and-trace and Verdier suppliers. The finite product-projection and coefficient-extension computations are otherwise choice-free.",
        "dependency_level": 17
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-analytic-constructible-sheaves-admit-coherent-six-operations",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Actual analytic constructible sheaves admit coherent six operations",
        "deps": [
          "def-algebraically-constructible-complex-of-analytic-field-sheaves",
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-compactly-supported-global-sections",
          "def-derived-category-of-an-abelian-category",
          "def-derived-hom-in-the-bounded-setting",
          "def-direct-image-sheaf",
          "def-extension-by-zero-abelian-sheaf",
          "def-inverse-image-presheaf-and-sheaf",
          "def-sheaf-hom",
          "def-sheaf-on-topological-space",
          "def-sheaf-tensor-product",
          "lem-complex-algebraic-stratifications-have-finite-conical-cochain-models",
          "lem-finite-simplicial-constructible-sheaves-have-a-derived-incidence-model",
          "thm-analytic-sheaf-six-operations-have-coherent-base-change-projection-and-trace",
          "thm-compactly-supported-derived-pushforward-has-exceptional-inverse-image-adjoint",
          "thm-verdier-duality-on-oriented-stratified-complex-varieties"
        ],
        "statement": "Assume AC ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]) and let $k$ be an arbitrary field. On separated finite-type complex varieties, the ordinary analytic sheaf operations restrict to bounded algebraically constructible complexes $D_c^b(-;k)$ ([[def-algebraically-constructible-complex-of-analytic-field-sheaves]]): $f^*\\dashv Rf_*$, $Rf_!\\dashv f^!$, the tensor/internal-Hom adjunction, coherent composition, support localization, ordinary and extraordinary proper base change, the projection formula and trace. Proper $f$ satisfies $Rf_!=Rf_*$. Verdier duality is involutive there and exchanges these adjoints. On a smooth complex $d$-fold $\\omega_X=k_X[2d]$, and for a smooth map of relative dimension $d$, $f^!=f^*[2d]$. Coefficient extensions commute with these operations on bounded constructible inputs. The bounded constructibility and finite coefficient models are those of [[lem-complex-algebraic-stratifications-have-finite-conical-cochain-models]] and [[lem-finite-simplicial-constructible-sheaves-have-a-derived-incidence-model]].",
        "strategy": "Assume AC. Sources: Bernstein-Lunts, Part I SS1.4.1-SS1.4.6 (tensor-Hom, composition, adjunctions, proper equality, open localization triangles and base change) and SS1.6-SS1.7 (dualizing object, Verdier duality for continuous maps, and smooth maps of relative dimension $d$), together with the finite resolution construction of Part I SS1.9/Appendices A and the derived-category simplicial comparison; BBD, Faisceaux pervers, SS1.4.1-1.4.10 (the recollement localization triangles giving localization and gluing), as an independent treatment. Step 1: the actual compact-support adjoint and coherent six-operation suppliers construct the functors and their adjunction units/counits, not just unrelated isomorphisms; their ordinary coherent composition, Cartesian exchange, projection/trace and localization diagrams are the asserted diagrams, including proper equality $Rf_!=Rf_*$ and the smooth local-product comparisons. All vector-space and injective constructions apply over an arbitrary field; their signed cochains use only $0$ and the units $\\pm1$, so no characteristic hypothesis enters. Step 2: the actual finite conical and incidence suppliers prove bounded constructibility and finite coefficient models for the stated finite collection, so the constructed operations restrict to $D_c^b$ and their finite local cochain comparisons commute with field extension; the actual support construction for compactly supported operations is used, and no infinite tensor of injective products is formed. Step 3: the oriented stratified Verdier supplier gives its evaluation isomorphism and identifies the dualizing object on a smooth complex $d$-fold with $k[2d]$ through the positive complex orientation; its adjunction construction gives duality exchange and the stated smooth extraordinary pullback $f^!=f^*[2d]$, and all these maps use the same ordinary units/counits and orientation, so their coherence is the coherence of the actual construction. The integral orientation generator maps to the nonzero unit $1\\in k$ over every field, including characteristic two.",
