      {
        "id": "lem-smooth-complex-pullback-is-exact-for-the-middle-perverse-t-structure",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Smooth complex pullback is exact for the middle perverse t structure",
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-derived-category-of-an-abelian-category",
          "def-direct-image-sheaf",
          "def-extension-by-zero-abelian-sheaf",
          "def-inverse-image-presheaf-and-sheaf",
          "def-sheaf-hom",
          "def-sheaf-on-topological-space",
          "lem-analytic-constructible-sheaves-admit-coherent-six-operations",
          "thm-complex-algebraic-varieties-and-maps-admit-compatible-finite-stratifications",
          "thm-ordinary-middle-perverse-t-structure-glues-and-has-simple-intersection-complexes"
        ],
        "statement": "Assume AC ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]) and let $a:X\\to Y$ be a smooth algebraic map of pure relative complex dimension $d$ between separated finite-type complex varieties, over an arbitrary coefficient field $k$. Then $a^*[d]$ is exact for the ordinary middle-perverse t structures of [[thm-ordinary-middle-perverse-t-structure-glues-and-has-simple-intersection-complexes]] on $D_c^b(-;k)$, and it commutes with their truncation and cohomology functors. Complex orientation gives $a^!=a^*[2d]$. If $a$ is surjective, its normalized pullback is conservative and reflects the perverse support and cosupport inequalities. The compatible finite stratifications used are those of [[thm-complex-algebraic-varieties-and-maps-admit-compatible-finite-stratifications]].",
        "strategy": "Assume AC. Sources: BBD, Faisceaux pervers, SS2.1.1-2.1.23 (the perverse t-structure on stratified spaces and its behavior under open/closed restriction and smooth strata); Bernstein-Lunts, Part I SS1.7 (smooth maps of relative dimension $d$ have invertible dualizing object, locally $C[d]$, so $f^!\\simeq f^*\\otimes D_f\\simeq f^*[d]$ up to the stated normalization) and SS1.4.3-1.4.4 (adjunctions and proper equality), as an independent treatment. Step 1 (upper aisle): on a smooth target stratum $S$ of complex dimension $e$, the nonempty smooth preimage strata have dimension $e+d$; exact inverse image gives $H^q(a^*A[d])=a^*H^{q+d}(A)$, and for $A$ in the upper middle-perverse aisle the right-hand side vanishes on these strata when $q+d>-e$, precisely when $q>-(e+d)$; local smooth product charts preserve the compatible target stratification ([[thm-complex-algebraic-varieties-and-maps-admit-compatible-finite-stratifications]]), so this proves preservation of the upper aisle. Step 2 (lower aisle): the ordinary six-operation construction gives $D_Xa^*=a^!D_Y$ and complex orientation gives $a^!=a^*[2d]$; hence $D_X(a^*A[d])=a^*D_YA[d]$, and since the ordinary middle-perverse core identifies the lower aisle as the dual of the upper aisle, Step 1 proves preservation of the lower aisle too. The orientation unit is nonzero over every field, exact finite-dimensional duality is field-general, and $[2d]$ is a cohomological shift, so the argument applies over arbitrary $k$. Step 3 (truncation and reflection): applying the t-exact functor to a truncation triangle produces the unique target truncation triangle, proving commutation with perverse truncations and cohomology; if $a$ is surjective, inverse image is stalkwise conservative and reflects ordinary cohomological vanishings, and the same dimension calculation applied to support and dual support reflects both perverse inequalities.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
